            <div xml:id="d699">

                <pb facs="0562" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg480"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1706.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul General
                        to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Monterey</hi></placeName> (Received <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-05-11">May 11, 1911</date>).</dateline></opener>
                <p>The worst thing happening in Mexico to-day is the foolish talk about American
                    military intervention. All believe such a thing at <pb facs="0563" n="481"
                        xml:id="pg481"/> present time would be a crime against the Americans in
                    Mexico as well as American interests. Please instruct me to instruct consuls
                    positively to deny such reports.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
